From a5519b2533cc939b668d254183333648bc9f174f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:33:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linux-swap: Detect encrypted swap files on btrfs

The subvolumes of a btrfs filesystem have anonymous device numbers that
have no block device, so neither udisks nor /sys/dev/block can resolve
the device a swap file is on, and a swap file on an encrypted btrfs was
reported as unencrypted.

Ask btrfs for the fsid of the filesystem instead, and check that each
of the devices /sys/fs/btrfs/<fsid>/devices lists has a crypt layer
below it, as a filesystem can span several devices.

Fixes https://github.com/fwupd/fwupd/issues/11154

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
